💭 ASTBinaryOperator::generateLogical() releases ordinary temporary objects after each operand of 🤝/👐. A receiver
💭 allocated for a pending initializer call must survive those checkpoints, since the initializer has not taken
💭 ownership of it yet, or it is released, and later used as if it still were valid, before it is even reached.
