    ↩️ v
  🍉

  💭 Neither operand reraises: this alone crashed before the fix, because the pending receiver was tracked as an
  💭 ordinary temporary and released after the left operand, before the initializer was ever reached.
  🐇❗️ 🙋 a 👌 b 👌 ➡️ 📦 🍇
    ↩️ 🆕📦 a 🤝 b❗️
  🍉

  💭 The right operand reraises after the left operand's temporary-release checkpoint already ran.
  🐇❗️ 🐝 a 👌 fail 👌 ➡️ 📦 🚧🚧 🍇
    ↩️ 🆕📦 a 🤝 🔺🥭🐇🐟 a fail❗️❗️
  🍉

  💭 The receiver of a nested construction, used as one initializer's first argument, must independently survive
  💭 the checkpoint hit while evaluating its own arguments, while the outer receiver, already pending, must too.
  🐇❗️ 🦋 a 👌 fail 👌 ➡️ 🎈 🚧🚧 🍇
    ↩️ 🆕🎈 🆕📦 a 🤝 🔺🥭🐇🐟 a fail❗️❗️ a❗️
  🍉
